      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Configure heartbeat model fallback policy",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nHeartbeat runs are unattended, but when the configured heartbeat model fails they fall through the general model fallback chain. Background automation then silently re-runs on a provider/model the operator never chose for it — e.g. a cheap heartbeat model failing over to the expensive primary every 30 minutes, or to a provider excluded from background work. There is no heartbeat-scoped fallback policy.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nCron already solves this for its jobs: payload `fallbacks`, where `[]` forces a strict run. This gives heartbeats the same control instead of changing any default. `heartbeat.fallbacks` is a sibling of `heartbeat.model` and threads through the existing per-run fallback override boundary (`FollowupRun.run.modelFallbacksOverride`), so an explicit `[]` reaches run construction and is never conflated with \"unset\".\n\n## User Impact\n\nOmitted `heartbeat.fallbacks` = existing fallback resolution, unchanged. Operators who want strict or heartbeat-specific fallback:\n\n```json5\n{\n  agents: {\n    defaults: {\n      heartbeat: {\n        model: \"provider/model\",\n        fallbacks: [], // fail fast; or [\"provider/model\", ...] for a heartbeat-specific chain\n      },\n    },\n  },\n}\n```\n\nPer-agent override: `agents.list[].heartbeat.fallbacks`. Config surface: `HeartbeatSchema.fallbacks` (zod), `AgentDefaultsConfig` types, schema help + labels, write-time model-ref normalization for the array, docs (`docs/gateway/heartbeat.md`, `docs/concepts/models.md`, `docs/concepts/model-failover.md`, `docs/gateway/config-agents.md` reference).\n\n## Evidence\n\nRebased onto current `main`. The reference-docs gap flagged in review (`config-agents.md` heartbeat block missing `fallbacks` / `[]` semantics) is fixed in this PR.\n\n- Post-rebase, all green (271 tests): `src/infra/heartbeat-runner.model-override.test.ts`, `src/auto-reply/reply/agent-runner-utils.test.ts`, `src/auto-reply/reply/get-reply-run.media-only.test.ts`, `src/config/io.write-prepare.test.ts`, `src/config/heartbeat-config-honor.inventory.test.ts`, `src/config/schema.base.generated.test.ts`, `src/config/schema.help.quality.test.ts`, `src/config/schema.test.ts`, `src/config/zod-schema.agent-defaults.test.ts`.\n- Behavior coverage: explicit `[]` override honored without re-resolution; heartbeats leave the override unset by default; embedded-run param passthrough; heartbeat config-key inventory includes `fallbacks`.\n- `pnpm tsgo:core` / `pnpm tsgo:core:test` clean for touched code; `pnpm docs:list`; `git diff --check`.\n\nAutoreview was explicitly skipped at user request for the original authoring; the post-rebase state was re-validated with the suites above.\n",
